00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The Witch (stylized as The VVitch, and subtitled A New-England Folktale) is a 2015 folk horror
film written and directed by Robert Eggers in his feature directorial debut.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
It stars Anya Taylor-Joy in her feature film debut, alongside Ralph Ineson,
Kate Dickie, Harvey Scrimshaw, Ellie Grainger, and Lucas Dawson.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Set in 1630s New England, the narrative follows a Puritan family who are
preyed upon by an evil force in the woods beyond their farm.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
In fear and desperation, they turn upon one another even when the
oldest daughter is suspected of being a witch.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
An international co-production of the United States and Canada, the film premiered at the Sundance
Film Festival on January 27, 2015, and was widely released by A24 on February 19, 2016.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It was a critical and financial success, grossing $40 million against a $4 million budget, and is
considered by some to be one of the best horror films of the 2010s and the 21st century.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film explores themes of witch, halloween, haunted house, prank.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The tone is dark.
